    test(ci): pytest-cov coverage tooling with measured baseline (INT-CI-2)
    
    - pyproject.toml: pytest-cov>=6 added to [dependency-groups].dev (resolves
      pytest-cov 7.1.0 + coverage 7.16.2 via uv).
    - Measured baseline on host venv 3.11: `pytest plugin -q --cov=terminal_jail
      --cov-report=term-missing` => TOTAL 75% (1255 stmts, 316 missed; 1510 passed,
      7 skipped). CI-shaped scope (plugin/ tests/, integration deselected) measures
      74.82%.
    - README Development > Coverage: command, both measured numbers (dated), honest
      caveats — tests excluded, 7 host-gated skips (bare-mode PID-NS conditionals,
      seccomp CAP_SYS_ADMIN, SIGHUP reload) leave their paths unmeasured, so the
      number is host-dependent; coverage is not assertion quality.
    - ci.yml test job: pip install pytest-cov; test step runs with
      --cov=terminal_jail --cov-report=term --cov-fail-under=74 (floor at/below
      both measured numbers; verified locally: exact CI-shaped invocation exits 0
      with "74% reached. Total coverage: 74.82%"; fail-under rc=1 behavior proven
      on a deliberate-trip probe).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
